      overview:['Begin by marking clause boundaries and conjunctions. Locate a finite verb or, in a verbless clause, the likely predicate. Separate inseparable prefixes and pronominal suffixes from their host. Identify construct chains and adjective relationships before assigning broader clause roles. Then parse person, gender, and number and propose the lexical root and stem.','If the form differs from the strong pattern, inspect it for weak-root behavior rather than guessing from one vowel. Consult the focused Paradigm Chart only after observing the visible clues. Finally produce a provisional reading that preserves the clause relationships, verbal sequence, and attached elements. Compare English afterward and revisit the exact feature that remains uncertain.'],
